EXTRA={
'NSE-DG-01':(['Stage KES 100,000 over three months','Retain cash for acquisition costs and whole-share rounding.','A core is a portfolio role with a review rule, not a universal ticker list.','Treat dividend sustainability and total return as related but distinct questions.'],['A whole-share order leaves residual cash','Use the saved reference price and its date.','Monthly allocation is rounded down to an affordable integer quantity.','Record both share cost and maximum modeled fees.'],['Trace the dividend into net household cash','Separate ordinary distributions from special payments.','Apply the relevant withholding assumptions explicitly.','Review payout, cash generation, debt and reinvestment before extrapolating income.']),
'NSE-DG-02':(['A watchlist is a research queue','Record why each candidate could fill a portfolio role.','A candidate may remain deferred while evidence is missing.','A new ticker does not automatically add a new economic exposure.'],['Compare the candidate with what you already own','Aggregate banks, sectors and shared operating drivers.','Include liquidity, cash needs and maximum position size.','Look through overlapping holdings before calling the portfolio diversified.'],['Make entry discipline inspectable','Record the price date, valuation range and source.','Set required evidence and the condition that rules out a purchase.','Review quarterly and after a material change; expire stale theses.']),
'USMPC-01':(['Start with the economic claim','A company operates a business; a security defines an investor claim.','An exchange is a trading venue, while an index is a rule-based measurement.','A fund holds assets under a mandate; a portfolio combines claims for a purpose.'],['Benchmarks answer different questions','A large-company benchmark differs from a broad market or growth-heavy benchmark.','Weighting rules affect whose returns dominate the result.','Compare total return, currency and time period on a consistent basis.'],['Risk has more than one dimension','Volatility measures variability, while a drawdown describes a peak-to-trough loss.','Liquidity affects whether an investor can transact at a useful price.','Match horizon, spending currency and acceptable loss before selecting a wrapper.']),
'USMPC-02':(['A wrapper changes implementation','Direct shares, mutual funds and ETFs package ownership differently.','Creation and redemption connect ETF shares with the underlying basket.','Legal structure, dealing mechanics and investor eligibility belong in the comparison.'],['Count four layers of cost','The fund expense ratio compounds inside the investment.','Spread, commissions and market impact affect execution.','Tax, currency conversion and funding affect what the household retains.'],['Make the fee comparison comparable','Keep the gross return, horizon and contributions the same.','Date each published fee and benchmark description.','Different exposures cannot be ranked solely by expense ratio.']),
'USMPC-03':(['Begin with the investor’s facts','Record residence, citizenship, account owner and relevant treaty position.','Separate the legal domicile from the exchange and dealing currency.','Trace the dividend from company through fund to investor.'],['Separate withholding from estate exposure','A payment-tax assumption does not resolve an ownership-at-death question.','Retain account, security and beneficiary records.','Use dated rules and investor-specific eligibility before implementing a route.'],['Currency belongs in the same record','Fund denomination and trading currency do not define every underlying exposure.','Match near-term cash obligations to their spending currency.','Compare custody, funding, reporting and exit costs as one implementation path.']),
'USMPC-04':(['Define jobs before tickers','A strategic core carries the enduring policy exposure.','A satellite takes a limited, explicit active risk.','Every sleeve needs a target, loss budget and decision authority.'],['Diversification depends on joint movement','Mixing equity and bonds changes both volatility and expected behaviour.','Portfolio standard deviation is not a weighted average of individual volatilities.','Correlation assumptions need a stress test when regimes change.'],['Architecture should constrain behaviour','Core-satellite, factor tilts and barbell designs make different commitments.','A concentrated sleeve needs a credible maximum-loss budget.','Choose a policy that the investor can fund, explain and maintain.']),
'USMPC-05':(['The benchmark comes before the ticker','SPYM provides S&P 500 exposure in the source comparison.','QQQM adds a deliberate Nasdaq-100 growth tilt.','A second fund may increase exposure to companies already held.'],['Look through the labels','Multiply fund weights by each underlying company weight.','Aggregate shared companies before assessing concentration.','Use HHI and effective holding count as diagnostics, not complete risk measures.'],['Contributions can repair drift','Send new cash to underweight sleeves before assuming a sale is needed.','Track spreads and liquidity alongside published fund fees.','Document the intended tilt and a maximum active weight.']),
'USMPC-06':(['Semiconductors are a concentrated industry exposure','SOXQ, SOXX, SMH and XSD use different eligibility and weighting rules.','Foundry, design, equipment and memory businesses have different drivers.','A low expense ratio does not remove cyclical or geopolitical risk.'],['The satellite overlaps the core','Aggregate company exposures across broad and thematic funds.','Weight concentration changes the impact of a single-company loss.','Test the semiconductor sleeve with growth and market exposures together.'],['Choose a loss budget before a theme','Size the sleeve using a plausible stress loss.','Set a target band and a thesis-break condition.','Record the evidence that would reduce, retain or exit the position.']),
'USMPC-07':(['A premium pays for an obligation','A cash-secured put may require buying the underlying at the strike.','A covered call limits upside while retaining downside ownership risk.','The underlying must be suitable even if assignment occurs.'],['Contract size creates concentration','One standard contract represents 100 shares in the source example.','Cash collateral is committed capital, not freely available reserve.','A small premium cannot offset an arbitrarily large underlying loss.'],['Evaluate the complete cycle','Include premiums, underlying price change, costs and taxes.','Do not annualise one favourable cycle as an expected return.','Benchmark the strategy against a consistent underlying and cash alternative.']),
'USMPC-08':(['Integrate all sleeves into one policy','The illustrative allocation combines core equity, bonds, a growth tilt and a satellite.','Look-through holdings reveal overlap hidden by the four labels.','Options collateral and cash reserves share the same balance sheet.'],['Risk contributions need a joint model','Volatility and correlations turn weights into portfolio variability.','A small volatile sleeve can contribute a larger share of risk.','Use scenario tables and review model assumptions before optimisation.'],['Rebalancing is a rule, not a prediction','Choose calendar, threshold or contribution-first triggers.','Calculate target trades using current total value.','Document costs, taxes, liquidity and the person authorised to trade.']),
'USMPC-09':(['Funding has its own timing decision','Lump-sum investment and staged contributions expose cash at different dates.','Keep the total amount and comparison horizon consistent.','The useful choice depends on cash needs, risk capacity and implementation.'],['Withdrawals make return order matter','The same set of annual returns can produce different ending balances.','Early losses plus withdrawals leave fewer assets to recover.','Test reserves, flexible spending and rebalancing together.'],['Maintenance is a household process','Revisit income, contributions, beneficiaries and near-term spending.','Separate documented policy changes from reactions to recent performance.','Preserve a review calendar and a decision record.']),
'LEAD-01':(['Map the dependency, not the personality','List decisions, customer relationships and operating knowledge held by one person.','Identify which work stops if the founder is unavailable.','Prioritise dependencies by time to disruption and business consequence.'],['Authority and access need separate controls','A deputy needs authority to act, not merely a password.','Preserve approvals, access recovery and legal signing arrangements.','Test handovers through real work with documented escalation.'],['Make continuity measurable','Build customer relationships beyond a single individual.','Use a short continuity plan with named deputies and contact routes.','Review performance through a ninety-day resilience programme.'])}
